{"cluster_id": "C-0254", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B012-015", "B012-080", "B012-089"], "canonical_claim": "Conditional `If-None-Match` and `If-Match` CAS writes perform exactly one HTTP attempt, using a request-scoped override so unrelated S3 disks retain their retry configuration. The underlying S3 client performs exactly one HTTP attempt for `If-None-Match` and `If-Match` writes, and a process-wide retry-count change is unacceptable if it alters unrelated S3 workloads. SDK-level retries must remain zero for conditional writes, and tests assert exact request counts so an invisible SDK retry fails the test.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L171-L179", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-s3-timeout-retry-control-rfc.md#disable-transparent-conditional-write-retries", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-s3-timeout-retry-control-rfc.md#failure-injection-tests", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-s3-timeout-retry-control-rfc.md#observability"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0255", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B012-016"], "canonical_claim": "Raw conditional-write results classify as `Committed` for 2xx, `DefiniteFailure` only for whitelisted malformed-request, entity-too-large, or access-denied classes, and `Unresolved` for timeout, connection loss, 5xx, or unresolved `PreconditionFailed`; `PreconditionFailed` is never a definite failure.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L171-L180"]}
