{"cluster_id": "C-0262", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B014-035", "B015-110"], "canonical_claim": "A dedup-cache hit does not skip the occupancy `HEAD`; it selects the `head_first` branch, and the `HEAD` runs precisely on hits, while the avoided operation is the body PUT counted by `CasBlobBodyPutAvoided`.; A dedup-cache hit does not skip the occupancy HEAD; it avoids the body PUT represented by `CasBlobBodyPutAvoided`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-14-cas-opt-levers-s1-s5.md#task-3-2-dedup-cache-sizing-measurement-no-cas-code", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-memory-s3-budget-optimizations-design.md#s2-dedup-cache"]}
