{"cluster_id": "C-0266", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B016-025", "B016-045"], "canonical_claim": "Compression is a deterministic per-type policy of `Never`, `Always`, or `PinnedRaw` with no size threshold; `cas_ref_log`, `cas_ref_snap`, `cas_part_manifest`, and `cas_gc_outcomes` are always compressed under a `.zst` key suffix, while `cas_run` and `cas_fold_seal` remain raw. The deterministic formats `cas_run` and `cas_fold_seal` are `PinnedRaw` and `Strict`, while the Always-compressed set is exactly `cas_ref_log`, `cas_ref_snap`, `cas_part_manifest`, and `cas_gc_outcomes`, whose `storedSuffix` is `.zst`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase1-formats-bootstrap.md#task-3", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-design.md#container-design"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0267", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B016-028"], "canonical_claim": "Additive CAS format evolution uses a new tolerant key, while breaking evolution requires a `v` bump, `G_BUILD`/`changePoints`, and write-down-to-floor; deterministic formats use strict keys and the adoption pin to re-encode at the existing object's version on a `putDeterministicArtifact` conflict.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-design.md#container-design"]}
